    <string name="disclosure_title">📍 Location, Activity &amp; Privacy Disclosure</string>
    <string name="disclosure_message">AirSlice accesses location, Wi-Fi, and physical activity step data on-device for Trip Mode and Saved Places (including in the background or with the screen off), and immediately discards almost all of it—keeping only movement speed (m/s) and GPS accuracy (m):\n\n• Saved Wi-Fi Places: Checks whether your connected Wi-Fi matches a Saved Place (Location permission required) so GPS and step sensing stay off at saved locations like your home or office, where movement tracking isn\'t needed.\n\n• Trip Movement (GPS + Steps): Outside Saved Places while your monitor is nearby, converts GPS fixes and hardware step cadence into scalar speed (m/s) and accuracy (m) in memory, immediately discarding raw coordinates and step counts.\n\n• 100% Local &amp; Private: Raw GPS coordinates, unconfigured Wi-Fi names, and step counts are never saved to disk or sent to any server; recorded summaries leave your phone only when you explicitly share an XLSX workbook or diagnostic log.</string>
    <string name="disclosure_continue_btn">Continue</string>
    <string name="disclosure_decline_btn">Not Now (BLE Only)</string>

    <string name="help_dialog_title">❓ AirSlice Help &amp; FAQ</string>
    <string name="help_intro">AirSlice is a 100% local, cloud-free Bluetooth companion and Trip Slicer for the Qingping Air Monitor Lite (CGDN1) and compatible BTHome v2 sensors.\n\n• With a CGDN1 Monitor: Turn on the monitor (or hold its top touchbar ~7s until the Wi-Fi icon appears if unconfigured). AirSlice completes offline Bluetooth setup in ~5s and records continuously—no cloud or account needed.\n\n• No Monitor Handy? (Testing &amp; Evaluation): Enable Demo Data Mode below to unlock a simulated live sensor stream on the Now tab and a sample multi-leg excursion on the Trips tab. You can also import shared .xlsx trip files.</string>
    <string name="help_demo_enabled_btn">✅ Demo Data Mode Enabled (Tap to Turn Off)</string>
